# Storage and recovery | Match data access to durability and transaction needs. | Choose storage for records, documents and temporary computation.
Objects and rows | Object stores address blobs by key; relational databases provide indexed queries and transactional constraints. Store document metadata separately when users need searchable attributes. | Object key; Row; Index | reports/42.pdf plus database row id=42,status=ready,key=reports/42.pdf | Query status in the database, download by object key. | Content platforms separate metadata and large files. | Reconcile a ready row with a missing object.
