? Which action triggers a computation? | count() | Variable assignment | Usually filter() alone | count requests an evaluated result.
? What may reduce shuffle payload? | Early valid filtering and projection | Extra unused columns | Changing chart colors | Narrower intermediates carry fewer bytes.
# Joins and skew | Prevent memory failures and long-tail partitions. | Compare small-dimension joins and a hot-key workload.
Broadcast choice | Replicate a genuinely small reference table to avoid shuffling both sides. Validate decoded memory size before forcing broadcast. | Broadcast; Dimension; Executor memory | Fact 200 GB, validated dimension 1 MB: consider broadcasting the dimension. | Workers match facts to the local reference copy. | Data marts enrich large transactions. | Explain when compressed file size understates in-memory size.
Hot keys | One heavily repeated key can dominate a single hash partition. Diagnose task sizes and duration, then consider special handling or a correctness-preserving skew strategy. | Skew; Straggler; Hash partition | Key A has 900,000 rows; all other keys total 100,000. | A's partition can dominate elapsed time. | Event pipelines see default anonymous identifiers. | Compare handling A separately with simply adding partitions.
